@@ -24,6 +24,28 @@ input throws `InvalidTaskError`, which carries the position of the first
 invalid item in `index`. All library errors extend `TaskPlanError` and have a
 `code`.

+## Planning
+
+The planning API computes an execution order and round-based stages for a set of tasks.
+
+```ts
+import { planOrder } from "./src/index.ts";
+```
+
+`planOrder(tasks)` returns a `PlanResult` with `order` and `stages`. Tasks are ordered by dependencies, with ties broken by `priority` (highest first) then input position. Stages group tasks by the earliest round they can run: a task with no dependencies is round 0, otherwise round 1 + max dependency round. Within a stage tasks are sorted by priority then input position.
+
+Errors are reported via `DuplicateTaskError`, `UnknownDependencyError` and `CycleError`, all extending `TaskPlanError`.
+
+The CLI provides the same functionality:
+
+```
+node src/cli.ts plan <file.json> [--json]
+```
+
+Default output prints stages and order; `--json` prints the `PlanResult` as JSON.
+
+See `examples/basic.ts` for a runnable example that uses `planOrder` and prints the plan in the default format.
+
 ## Development

 Requires Node.js 24 or later. TypeScript files run directly with Node.
